{title: Revive Us Again}
{artist: William P. Mackay / John Husband}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{key_original: G}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]We praise Thee, O God, for the Son of Thy love
For [A7]Jesus who died and is [D]now gone above
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Hallelujah, Thine the glory, hallelujah, A[A7]men
Hallelujah, Thine the glory, re[D]vive us a[A7]gain[D]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]We praise Thee, O God, for Thy Spirit of light
Who has [A7]shown us our Savior and [D]scattered our night
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]All glory and praise to the Lamb that was slain
Who has [A7]borne all our sins and has [D]cleansed every stain
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
